# Upstream defaults, written literally. lazygit's keys live in config.yml under
# a nested `keybinding:` tree, and a config that has never been edited does not
# contain them at all — so there is nothing to read back until you rebind
# something. The SCAN tab generates a probed file if you do.
name:    lazygit
what:    git as a UI. Stage by hunk with arrow keys instead of git add -p
check:   lazygit
install: sudo dnf install lazygit   /   see github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit
docs:    ? inside it lists every key for the panel you are in

= THE IDEA
Tab              | next panel: Status, Files, Branches, Commits, Stash
Shift-Tab        | previous panel
1 2 3 4 5        | jump straight to a panel by number
?                | every key for the panel you are in. Start here
q                | quit
Esc              | back out of a menu or a diff
mouse            | click a panel, click a file, scroll a diff

= FILES PANEL — where you will spend the time
Space            | stage or unstage the file under the cursor
a                | stage or unstage everything
Enter            | open the file's hunks, to stage part of it
Space (in hunks) | stage just this hunk
d                | discard the change. There is a confirmation
c                | commit what is staged
A                | amend the last commit with what is staged
e                | open the file in your editor
s                | stash everything

= COMMITS PANEL
Enter            | see what the commit changed, file by file
d                | drop the commit (interactive rebase)
r                | reword its message
s                | squash it into the one below
f                | fixup into the one below
Ctrl-j / Ctrl-k  | move the commit down or up in history
R                | revert it as a new commit

= BRANCHES PANEL
Space            | check out the branch under the cursor
n                | new branch from here
d                | delete it
r                | rebase the current branch onto this one
M                | merge this one into the current branch
f                | fetch

= STASH PANEL
Space            | apply the stash
g                | pop it
d                | drop it

= PUSHING AND PULLING
p                | pull
P                | push
Shift-P          | force push, with a confirmation
